cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Soga in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Soga: C++ and Arduino programming in the written languages of South Africa"
abstract: >-
  Soga is C++ with its vocabulary in the ten written official languages of South Africa
  (isiZulu, isiXhosa, siSwati, isiNdebele, Sesotho, Setswana, Sepedi, Xitsonga, Tshivenda and Afrikaans).
  It is a source-to-source translator to standard C++, so programs build into the same machine code as the
  C++ they stand for. It includes a command-line tool, a language server, a Visual Studio Code extension,
  an Arduino IDE library, compiler messages in all ten languages, and a 103-lesson Arduino textbook.
